{
  "requirement": "The method is declared under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.running-criteria.store_evidence`.\n\nThe method saves under the source identity and criterion path captured in\n`Fingerprinted`, preserving its version, input trace, and completed answer. Encoding follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record.output`; atomic replacement follows\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.evidence_storage`. The result type needs\nno `Sync` bound: the method encodes the answer and captures the record and\nstorage key before constructing the storage future.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.store_evidence`. I did not read the implementation, and I did not reassess the cited requirements' own tests.\n\nObligation-to-test mapping:\n- **Saves under the source identity and criterion path from `Fingerprinted`.** `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` in `tests/contracts.rs` stores values and reloads them by source and criterion. It also looks up the saved records by criterion path (`behavior`, `text`) and asserts their output. `serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged` and `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` load directly by `(Node(1), path)` through the domain. `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors` stores through `FileEvidenceStorage` and reads the record at the path derived from the source and criterion.\n- **Preserves version, input trace and completed answer.**\n  - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` compares the loaded output, source, path, version and dependencies with the stored value.\n  - `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` asserts that the stored dependencies are the new `Dependency::Node(2, ...)` fingerprint.\n  - `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` asserts that the saved version, dependencies and output all come from the same save.\n  - `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer` and `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets` (both in `agent/tests.rs`) assert saved dependencies, including `OutgoingEdges`, against the stored value.\n  - `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` in `validation_tests.rs` asserts the stored dependencies.\n- **Replacement of an existing record.** `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence` stores a v2 value over a v1 record and asserts that one record remains. `input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations` asserts that the stored dependencies are replaced.\n- **Encoding follows `record.output`.**\n  - A serialization failure returns `ValidationError::Output` and leaves the existing record unchanged. `serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged` asserts the error variant and message. It asserts that version, dependencies and output are unchanged, and that the write count is still 1.\n  - A storage failure returns `ValidationError::Graph`. `resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments` in `validation_tests.rs` sets `fail_store` and asserts `Graph(\"store\")` and that no record exists.\n- **Atomic replacement follows `evidence_storage`.** The concurrent-store test asserts that the saved record is complete and from a single save. This obligation is also delegated to the cited requirement.\n- **No `Sync` bound on the result type, and the future is `Send`.** `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` stores a non-`Sync` `Cell` answer through the `send(...)` helper and then reloads it.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "8561f0acb4fa06d2bcf449879c6c18e3a9f1c4c2cfce0597b732e72399ab8b47",
